                "instr": "Questions 31–36<br>Complete the notes below.<br>Write <b>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</b> for each answer.",
                "type": "html",
                "html": "<h4 class=\"center\">The archaeological site of Trimera</h4><p><b>Location</b></p><ul><li>southern Europe</li><li>mountainous region overlooking a plain</li></ul><p><b>History</b></p><ul><li>12,000 years ago: hunter-gatherers lived in area</li><li>5,000 years ago: farmers lived on banks of the rivers</li><li>2,500 years ago: became a trade centre</li><li>300 BC: invaded by Greeks</li><li>100 BC: invaded by Romans – trade in grain, olives and [[31]]</li><li>518 AD: city abandoned following earthquake</li></ul><p><b>Rediscovery of site</b></p><ul><li>1706: French explorer believed the site was the remains of a [[32]]</li><li>19th century: a map was made of the site</li><li>1982: a complete [[33]] was made</li></ul><p><b>Excavation</b></p><ul><li>the [[34]] was the first place to be excavated</li><li>a number of [[35]] were discovered</li><li>evidence of a [[36]] industry was found</li></ul>"
