                "instr": "Questions 31–39<br>Complete the table below.<br>Write <b>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</b> for each answer.",
                "type": "html",
                "html": "<h4 class=\"center\">Research in child psychology</h4><table class=\"grid\"><tr><th>Past</th><th>Present</th></tr><tr><td>Three aspects of development: social, cognitive, emotional.</td><td>These aspects now regarded as being [[31]].</td></tr><tr><td>Behaviour was studied in artificial contexts.<br>Example: [[32]] (was related to behaviour of animals in [[33]])</td><td>Awareness that child's behaviour is influenced by his/her [[34]] and the situation he/she is in.</td></tr><tr><td>Child was seen as being [[35]].<br>Parents were held responsible for way child developed.</td><td>No direct link between early influences and child's [[36]].</td></tr><tr><td>Influence of Piaget:<br>Young children were believed to be [[37]].</td><td>Influence of Harriet Rheingold:<br>Examples show that children are aware of other people.</td></tr><tr><td>Psychologists did not take culture into account.<br>Example: importance of [[38]] for babies.</td><td>Guatemalan study – babies are kept in the [[39]] – no effect on later development.</td></tr></table>"
